C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f1\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f2\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\\f3\\fswiss\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f4\\fswiss\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\\f5\\fnil Courier New;}{\\f6\\fnil\\fcharset0 Courier New;}}
{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs16 Change Log\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 V71-5/11/23:\\cf0\\f2\\fs22\\par
\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 1.  Changed the cutout logic for the Temperature controller to be uOEMOnTime>30 min, then release control to tstat until next tstat cycle. \\cf0\\f2\\fs22\\par
\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 v70-5/9/23:\\cf0\\f2\\fs22\\par
\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 1.  In the Time Temperature Load Cotnroller made the following changes:\\cf0\\f2\\fs22\\par
\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 a.  Removed the delay with the IC = 1 and used a merge block instead (in case the codegen was not picking up the ID).\\cf0\\f2\\fs22\\par
\\pard\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 b.  added logic to the merges for online/offline, added uOEM Ontime < 10 and added IsBypassFromCloud.  the uOEM ontime prevents the use of the min values when there is 0 uOEM runtime.  Adding the isBypassFromCloud prevented cycling if \\f3\\par
\\par
V69 - 5/7/23:\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720 1.\\tab Added an additional load controller \\ldblquote Time Temperature Controller\\rdblquote .  On alternate OEM cycles, this controller put itself offline and measured the OEM ON and OFF times.  Then, on the following cycle, this controller put itself online and set its ON time to be an onTimeFraction* OEM ON time measured during the previous cycle.  The onTimeFraction is calculated linearly from the errorRAT, when the errorRAT is small, the onTimeFraction is small and Pace ON time is small and the OFF time is large.  Both the ON and OFF times are limited to lie between Normal and Extend values.  When the errorRAT is large, the onTimeFraction is large and the ON is extended and OFF time reduced.  \\par
2.\\tab Cyclers were simplified by removing the limiter on yPace (this was causing problems with the logic in 1. Above).  Also the calculation of uPace was simplified and no longer creates a tDelay value.  \\par
\\pard\\par
v68 - 5/4/23:\\par
1.  set tDelay on ch3 to 999 and modified the ch3 cycler AND with third input (see v64).  This will prevent ch3 from coming on when the Pace is online.\\par
\\par
V67 - 5/4/23:\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720 1.\\tab Removed \\ldblquote Pulse2Gate\\rdblquote  in the 5 cyclers\\par
2.\\tab Removed uOEMOnTime>=tDelay to the AND in each of the 5 cyclers (to ensure there is no tDelay)\\par
3.\\tab Added 2 delay debounce to yPace on each cycler to prevent 1 second OFF then ON when bypass turns off\\par
4.\\tab Set FRACTION_SAT_ERROR = 0 (run on RAT error only)\\par
5.\\tab Added a gain of 5 on temperatureErrorGBL (lengthen tOn at smaller temperature errors)\\par
6.\\tab Calculate the temperature setpoint at 8AM and use for the entire day (increased temperature error = longer ON times)\\par
\\pard\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\par
v66 - 5/3/23:\\par
1.  Remove the 1 hour \"release to thermostat\" logic in each of the 5 cyclers, temperature control.\\par
2.  Remove the forced bypass times, do no go to forced bypass ever. \\par
3.  modified the temperature setpoint calculation to occur every 3 hours using a LPF instead of RLS\\par
4.  corrected limiter on tOff in each of the load controllers, it was holding the min value.\\par
\\par
v65 was a TEST ONLY version, not for release\\par
\\par
v64 - 4/28/23:\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720\\cf1\\f3\\fs18 1.\\tab  Disabled Master Slave - for cypress we do not want to add any delay to the slave compressors, from the data collection it looks like the Trane controller already adds 180 seconds of delay to a slave.  \\par
2.\\tab Change the forced offline times to occur at 8AM and 2PM for 1 hour each\\par
3.\\tab When establishing the temperature setpoints during the forced offline times, check that the compressors are running before using the measured setpoint, if there is no compressor runtime, use the setpoints from the previous forced offline time.  Initialize SAT = 50degF and RAT = 70 degF at power up. \\par
4.  Changed timer reset to uOEOMFE instead of uOEMFE OR inputSignalRE in \"temperature controller cutout logic\" to eliminate the short open relay command that Tom W. has seen\\par
\\pard\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
v63 - 4/25/23:\\par
1.  Added time cutout if uOEM ON for > 3600 sec to the existing Temperature cutout logic.  This puts the unit into bypass based on the time the uOEM has been ON (3600 seconds).  This logic was added in addition to the 3deg 30 min logic.\\par
2.  In the Temperature cutout logic changed sat and rat to their average values.\\par
3.  Added RLS to temp calculations to get the average sat and rat\\par
4. Added the Min On and Off time logic and moved it to the yPace output in each cycler.\\par
\\par
v62 - 4/24/23:\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720\\cf1\\f3\\fs18 1.\\tab Modified the \\ldblquote Cycler Controller\\rdblquote  to create the \\ldblquote yPace\\rdblquote  command signal incuding the bypass logic.  This was done to address the issue Tom W has seen where the Pace is offline and for no apparent reason, cycles OFF for 3 or 4 minutes then turning back ON causing the compressor to cycle.  The Android OS has been combining the bypass logic with the pace command, now this calculation is done within the algorithm: if the channel is bypassed (internally or from the GUI or Cloud), the relay is set closed and output as the \\ldblquote yPaceOutput\\rdblquote , otherwise \\ldblquote yPace\\rdblquote  (the cycled output) is output as \\ldblquote yPaceOutput\\rdblquote . Removed the downstream block that applied the bypass logic. \\par
2.\\tab Removed the Key\\par
3.\\tab Removed Min On and Off time from cyclers\\par
4.\\tab Corrected the min ON and OFF time limiters used in each cycler to prevent short cycles which were observed on Cypress.  Now the default time values (nominal) are used instead of the calculated ON and OFF times (which are created based on the temperature errors)\\par
\\pard\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\cf1\\f3\\fs18 v61 - 4/16/23:\\par
1. fix master slave time delay reversal in logic\\par
2. in each of the 5 cycle controllers, replace the logic used to set \"isBypassFromGUI\" with the single \"\\f0 isBypassFromCloudPortalGBL\" defined in the \"Unload Inputs into Globals\" compound block (confirmed with Tom M that when an offline cmd is sent from the cloud, all 5 channels on the Pace GUI display bypassed)\\f3\\par
3. set slave time delay to 180 instead of 300 seconds. \\par
4.  added \"abs\" to the 3 deg temp error in the cycler cutout logic for temperature based control\\par
\\par
V60 - 4/13/23:\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720 1.\\tab Set \\ldblquote FRACTION_SAT_ERROR\\rdblquote  = .2 (was .5)\\par
2.\\tab Set \\ldblquote MasterSlaveControllerEnableGBL\\rdblquote  = 1 (on) and \\ldblquote MsterSlaveControllerSlaveTimeDelay\\rdblquote  = 300 sec (5 min)\\par
\\pard\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\par
V59 - 4/11/23:\\par
1.  On a daily basis at midnight, the Pace node reboots itself.  We tested this reboot and confirmed that the \\ldblquote powerUpFlagGBL\\rdblquote  does produce 3 high pulses (1 second each) right after the midnight reboot and then turns off (low) until the next midnight event.  A reset timer was added that is reset to 0 seconds when \\ldblquote powerUpFlagGBL\\rdblquote  goes high and then counts in seconds until the next midnight event where it is reset to 0.  The output of the time is \\ldblquote secondsPastMidnightGBL\\rdblquote  and the \\ldblquote timer2\\rdblquote  attached to the \\ldblquote midnightPulseGBL\\rdblquote  signal is removed.  isForcedBypassGBL gate signal created using the \\ldblquote powerUpFlag\\rdblquote  (which was tested to reset daily at midnight in v58 test by Tom W) is used to run a timer that creates  a gate signal \\ldblquote isForcedBypassGBL\\rdblquote  at 1AM and 1PM in \\ldblquote Bypass Signal\\rdblquote .  \\ldblquote isForcedBypassGBL\\rdblquote  is used in \\ldblquote Temperature Setpoint\\rdblquote  to calculate the \\ldblquote temperatureErrorGBL\\rdblquote  signal which is limited to lie between -1 and +1 and used directly in the channel temperature load controllers (all 5 of them)\\par
\\par
2. offline periods and calculations:  Use the \\ldblquote\\cf1\\f3\\fs18 secondsPastMidnightGBL\\rdblquote  timer to schedule two 1 hour offLine periods daily.  First period begins at 1AM to 2AM, second period begins at 1PM to 2PM.  During each period the following measurements are made: MaxSAT, MinSAT, MaxRAT, MinRat, Ontime and Offtime for each of the 5 channels. \\par
\\par
SAT and RAT setpoints are calculated as 0.5*(Max+Min). These setpoints are used until the next offline period.  Setpoint errors (SAT - setpointSAT) and (RAT - setpointRAT) are normalized to lie between  -1 to 1 by dividing each error by 0.5*(Max-Min).  The resulting normalized setpoint errors are named errorSAT and errorRAT.  A single temperature error is calculated = (fractionSATerror * errorSAT) + ((1-fractionSATerror)*errorRAT), where fractionSATerror is hardcoded to a value between 0 and 1 (.5 is used in v59).   When fractionSATerror = 1, the temperature error = SAT setpoint error, when fractionSATerror = 0, the temperature error = RAT setpoint error.  \\par
\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
3.  Only Ch1 apptype is used to determine whether all 5 channels are in heating or cooling mode.  The apptype for ch2,3,4,5 is ignored. The apptype is made GBL\\par
\\par
4.  tOn cooling range changed to 4 to 15.2 min, tOff = 3 to 4 min, tDelay = 0 for all cooling, master slave is set to not active for light and normal loads. These values are hardcoded into the Time Table CB. \\par
\\par
5. Master Slave:  added the enable/disable logic to \\ldblquote Set Slave time delays\\rdblquote  block in Master Slave, Only using the ch1 slave time delay for the MS additional time delay (it was set to 420 seconds when enabled from the GUI).  All master slave channel numbers no longer used in the \\ldblquote unload config vec\\rdblquote  block.  Master Slave is disabled in v59\\par
\\par
6. Removed code to allow SAT and RAT to be reversed when RATTemperatureSensorNumberGBL = 1. Set RATTemperatureSensorNumberGBL in \\ldblquote unload config vec\\rdblquote  = 0 (not used anywhere now). \\par
\\par
7. Included logic to change the sign\\rquote s of the setpoints in \\ldblquote Temperature Setpoint\\rdblquote  CB for heating and cooling.  A + error indicated either undercooling (too hot) or underheating (too cold). \\par
\\par
8.  Are RAT and SAT sensors reading correctly added to Unload Inputs into Globals and sent to the global variable \\ldblquote isRATAndSATOkGBL\\par
\\par
\\cf1\\f3\\fs18 The OEM signal on and off time measurements when the unit in in ForcedBypass are implemented in v59 but the light and normal load logic is not used.\\par
OntimeTotal = sum(ontime ch1, ch2, ch3, ch4, ch5) and OfftimeTotal = sum(offtime ch1, ch2, ch3, ch4, ch5).  Then the load is estimated with this logic\\par
Light load:  if ontime < .5*offtime\\par
Normal load: if  ontime >= .5* offtime\\par
\\par
Temperature controllers - possible logic (not implemented) \\par
If light load: tOn (initial) = .8* measured ontime for the channel, tOff = .2*measured ontime for the channel. tDelay = 0.  \\par
After being initialized, tOn and tOff will be controlled by the temperature error (tDelay will remain = 0).   Master Slave is not active for overlapping channels (because it is not likely that there will be overlapping channels)\\cf0\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\par
v58 - 3/26/23:\\par
1.  Updated master slave, only identified the master channel, no slaves channels are identified.  The  master channel is idenfied using the largest value of uOEMOnTime, all other channels are treated as slaves assuming they overlap with the master channel ON. \\par
2.  Created a SAT controller, now there is a RAT, SAT, and Time based controller, hardcoded to run the SAT controller\\par
3.  Kept the cooling times the same as v56; tVecNormal = [180, 240, 180], tVecExtend = [180, 576, 180]\\par
4.  Hardcoded all sensor enables to ON (thermostats, all temp sensors and ct)\\par
5.  \\f0\\fs18 master slave controller always ON\\par
6.  slave delays are all fixed at 420 seconds\\par
7.  control temperature sensor is set based on whether you use RAT or SAT control within the algorithm, cannot be set from the UI\\par
8.  SAT normalization factor = 10, RAT normalization factor = 1, hardcoded\\par
9.  lambda = .9995 in the temperature setpoint estimator for both RAT and SAT control, hardcoded\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\par
v57 - 3/20/23:  \\par
1.  Same as v56 but tOn Extend = 6.5 min instead of 4 min\\par
2.  Fixed the abs(SAT -RAT) < 3deg for 2 hour bypass until tstat next cycle, removed the s/h logic, now it goes to bypass if this condition is met and comes back online as soon as the tstat cycles.\\par
\\par
V56 - 3/17/23: Test version for low loads, Identical to v54 but with the following changes\\par
1.  Lead compressor has tDelay = 3 min, tOn = 4 min (normal and extend), tOff = 3 min(normal and extend)\\par
2.  Slave compressors have tDelay = 10 min total, same tOn and tOff as lead. \\par
\\par
v55 - 3/16/23: Test version for low loads, Identical to v54 but with the following changes\\par
1.  Lead compressor has tDelay = 0, tOn = 4 min (normal and extend), tOff = 3 min(normal and extend)\\par
2.  Slave compressors have tDelay = 10 min total, same tOn and tOff as lead. \\par
THIS VERSION WAS CORRUPTED, IT WAS NOT BUILT CORRECTLY AND REPORTED ITSELF AS V54 - DO NOT USE THIS\\par
\\par
\\par
v54 - 3/13/23:  identical to v53 except version changed from 53 to 54 because Tom W can only OTA not using the \"-r\" option in adb. \\par
\\par
v53 - 3/11/23: identical to v52 but reworked the master slave logic only; to not conditionally executed compound blocks with vector inputs.  I removed all of these and used s->v and v->s (I don't think the indexed assign and index blocks work correctly in codegen) and also reduced the number of vector variables by connecting vectors directly to compound blocks. This version compiled w/o errors and loaded and ran on the pace.  In this version the master slave is on permanently with a fixed 150 sec delay on each of the slave channels.  None of the UI controls work on the master slave.  This is the version sent to Tom W. for the texas trials in March of 2023.  \\par
\\par
v52 - 3/11/23: All changes based on v48, build with Embed 2020.3 build 57 (installed in Altair/Embed2020)/  This version compiled w/o errors but would not download and run on the Pace4.  After experimenting with a working previous version I found that adding in the new master slave block was causing this problem.  The changes I made to fix it are in version 53.\\par
1. Entirely new master slave logic.  slave delay for all slave channels hardcoded to 150 sec (which becomes 330 seconds when added to the tDelay) and the master slave enable is hardcoded ON.  None of the UI MasterSlave settings work in this version.  Had to eliminate all indexed assign blocks and used s->v and v->s instead (gave compile error creating .so files if I did not)\\par
2.  tVec = [180, 330, 210, 180, 576, 180]\\par
\\par
V50 - 2/25/23:  All changes based on v48, build with Embed 2020.3 build 57 (installed in Altair/Embed2020)\\par
1.  Redefine tDelay from 240 to 120 seconds (the greater value was causing LP alarms at the cypress site in Texas on large trane units)\\par
\\par
\\par
V49 - 1/22/23:  All changes based on v48, build with Embed 2020.3 build 57 (installed in Altair/Embed2020)\\par
1.  Redefine the tOffNormal from 390 to 330 seconds\\par
2. changed limits in \"isAlgorithmActive\" CB to 700 and 880 to accomodate the new lower tOn normal value\\par
\\f0\\fs16\\par
\\par
v48 - 1/5/23:  (all modifications were based on v45,  v46 and v47 were not used in any way)\\par
1.  Reworked Master Slave controller, now the input to a slave channel is the uMaster (thermostat cmd) AND'D with the uSlave (thermostat Cmd), it use to be only the uMaster cmd was applied to the slave channel.  This change was made to each of the \"Slavex\" CB's\\par
2.  Increased the Master/slave time delay from 200 to 1000 seconds on each of the 4 slave channels\\par
3.  Redefined tDelayNormal from 180 to 240 seconds for cooling only apptype\\par
4.  Redefined tOffNormal from 180 to 210 seconds for cooling only apptype\\par
5. changed limits in \"isAlgorithmActive\" CB to 800 and 880 to accomodate the tDelay and tOff changes above (otherwise the algorithm would remain offline)\\par
6.  Setpoint temperature calculation - added a setpoint reset equal to RLS value when all thermostat signals transition to OFF\\par
\\par
v45 - 6/22/20\\par
1.  Reworked the temperature setpoint calculation to repeat every 3 hours while in bypass.  More likely to get the right setpoint when the node is put online provided it occurs late in the afternoon of a workday.  \\par
2.  Removed firstPassFlag, only use Powerup flag\\par
3.  Reworked the average temperature calculation to be RLS with fading memory\\par
4.  Removed the manual setting to extend the tOn (but kept the input signal, it is not used in the algorithm)\\par
5.  Reworked isBypassFromCloudPortal, removed the 3 minute delay for midnight reset so it works more responsively, took care of the midnight reset in the temperature setpoint calculation, a new setpoint is only calculated if the node has been in bypass > 4 minutes. \\par
6.  Removed the PI from the load controller, now it works based on temperature error divided by a \"span\" set to 1 deg to produce the \"fractionLimited\" value.  \\par
7.  Changed the 0.5amp CT scaling to 5amp CT (scaling set to .12) and changed the GUI\\par
8.  In the data sent to the portal, enclosure temp = setpoint temperature and OAT = average temperature\\par
9.   midnight pulse is not used and time since midnight is not calculated\\par
10. AlgoStatusVec calculations remain but disconnected to reduce codegen size\\par
11. Added time based load control\\par
12 parameter vector modified;\\par
     a. removed NativeTimeDelayControlerEnable (it's always enabled but can be set to 0)\\par
     b. added paceCycleSetpoint (limited to 2 to 10 in increments of .05) fed into the GUI as 4 bits\\par
     c. added temperature span (nominal value = 1, limiited between .25 and 3) fed into the GUI as 4 bits\\par
     d.  The 4 bit values from b. and c. above are combined into a single 8 bit value, the decimal equivalent is sent into the algorithm (see below)\\par
\\fs18           cycleCount must line in the range [1:.5:5]  (MUST BE A MULTIPLE OF .5)\\par
           factor must lie in the range [.125:.125:1.875] (MUST BE A MULTIPLE OF .125)\\par
           FactorCycleCountValue= (8*factor) + (32*cycleCount)  - this must be done manually and entered into the GUI\\par
13 added cutout logic for domestic hot water heater SAT < 120degF to cyclers\\par
14 added minimum On and minimum Off time control downstream of each cycler and removed the debounce2 function\\fs16\\par
15.  Admin, username = Admin, pw = aaa\\par
\\par
v43.3\\par
\\pard\\box\\brdrdash\\brdrw0 \\cbpat2 1.  Modifications to HardwareStateUpdateService.java and PaceNativeHarness.c to feed the 5 channel bypass status values into the algorithm.  Now you can either set all 5 channels online or bypass from the cloud OR individually from the UI\\par
2. Modification to JAVA code to transmit the correct node status (online or bypass) to the pace cloud portal\\par
\\pard\\par
v43.2\\par
1.  Included a 5 minute timer on the \"isBypassFromCloudPortalGBL\" signal in \"Unload Inputs into Globals\" to prevent the temperature setpoint from being recalculated when the node is cycled at midnight daily from online to bypass then back to online.  The midnight cycle takes about 2 minutes to complete, 2.5 minutes is used as a safe value.\\par
\\par
v43.1\\par
1.  Modified Channel Controller logic, removed \"isLoadControllerBypassed\" flag (always set = 0) and forced tExtend if FeedbackTemp is failed OR TemperatureSetpoint is not ready.\\par
2.  Modified Measure SEtpoint Temperature block isTempSetpointReady output, now it requires the temp sensor to be valid, if not, isTempSetpointReady remains = 0\\par
\\par
\\par
v43\\par
1.  change the bit packed nodeStatus vector elements, removed load controller integrator status and replaced with isChxCorrelated (5 channels)\\par
2.  changed the current scaling gains, changed the 25amp CT to 0.5 amp CT, set default to 100 amp CT\\par
\\par
v42p7S2\\par
1.  changed the bit packed nodeStatus vector elements\\par
2.  changed the nodeStatus output to Long instead of float\\par
\\par
v42p7S1\\par
1.  In the 3 rate limit blocks in each of the 5 cyclers, changed the firstPassFlagGBL to powerUpFlagGBL\\par
2.  Added element 13 \"LoadControllerTemperatureSensorNumber\" to the config vector, changed the config vector to 13 elements throughout the algo and used this sensor number to specify the temperatrue feedback sensor.\\par
3.  Added \"isLoadControllerTemperatureSensorFailed\" to status output\\par
4.  Refrigeration timeVec changed from [240, 372, 240, 186, 480, 186] to [240,480,240, 180, 660, 180]\\par
5.  Added channel correlation with uOEM calculation to status vector\\par
\\par
\\par
\\par
v42p7S\\par
1. renamed \"proof\" to \"debounce2\" in cycler (short cycle controller removed)\\par
2.  removed tOffCoolingGBL and tOffHeatingGBL from Temperature Calculations, they are not used.\\par
3.  removed RLS from average temperature calculation\\par
4.  added is algo active function to cyclers\\par
5.  renamed variables to be consistent with uOEM, yPace, uOEMOnTime, ... (no functional changes, just made names the same)\\par
6.  added deltaSetpointGBL = .3 degF to heating and cooling in each of the 5 load controllers.  \\par
7.  connected algoStatusVec (4x1) to CommArrayOut elements 0,1,2,3 in PaceNativeHarness.c\\par
\\par
v42p7R\\par
1.  average temperature calculation modification:  removed the RLS of 5 cycles, it was responding too slowly.  Now the average temeprture is calculated when the Node is switched from bypass to online (setting any one channel to online forces the Node into online).  At the instant the Node enters online, the average temp is set to the RAT value, then it is averaged over 1 temperature cycle using isMax.  The total number of iterations is also limited to 10,000, then a reset is forced (about 3 hours)\\par
2.  Load controller sensor number is hardcoded to be temp2 (RAT), you must connect RAT to temp2 and SAT to temp1\\par
3.  \\cf1\\fs18 algoStatusVecGBL element 1 \\cf0\\fs16 changed to 25 elements;\\par
DryContact (1/0 = closed/open)\\par
temp1 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
temp2 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
temp3 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
OAT status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
enclosure temp status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
isTempSetpointReady (1/0 = yes/ no)\\par
not used\\par
relay1 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay2 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay3 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay4 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay5 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
isBypassCmdFromCloud (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isBypassCmdFromGUICh1 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isBypassCmdFromGUICh2 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isBypassCmdFromGUICh3 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isBypassCmdFromGUICh4 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isBypassCmdFromGUICh5 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isAlgoBypassCh1 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isAlgoBypassCh2 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isAlgoBypassCh3 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isAlgoBypassCh4 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
isAlgoBypassCh5 (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
\\par
Elements 2,3,4 are unchanged \\par
tempSetpointValue\\par
tempAverageValue\\par
Algorithm Version Number\\par
\\par
v42p7q\\par
1.  removed span entirely from the load calculation\\par
2.  removed short cycle controller from cycler, the behavior was not correct when the tstat cycled from off to on (not from a cold start), it imposed a long delay.  \\par
3.  changed the average temp and setpoint temp calculation from \"peak\" based to time based, the setpoint is calculated while all channels are in bypass, and held at that value when one or mor channels go online.  (logic in 4 and 5)\\par
\\par
\\fs18 4.  setpoint temperature (temp =RAT) calculation\\par
\\tab A = Node is bypassed (all 5 channels) AND\\par
 \\tab [(both a Min and Max temp value has occured) OR \\tab\\par
\\tab (sampleCountMax is exceeded) OR\\par
\\tab (isMax has occured)]\\par
\\par
\\tab tempSetpoint = Sample/Hold the AverageTemperature \\tab\\par
\\tab when one or more channels change to online OR RE(A).\\par
\\par
\\tab if Average Temperature = 0 (no setpoint calculated), then\\par
\\tab tempSetpoint = measured temperature\\par
\\par
\\tab if the temperature sensor is failed or absent, then \\par
\\tab tempSetpoint = AVG_AND_SETPOINT_TEMP_ON_FAILURE = 70 degF\\par
\\par
\\tab isTempSetpointReady \\par
\\tab set to 0 (not ready) at powerUp OR when Node goes into bypass (all 5 channels)\\par
\\tab set to 1 (ready) when one or more channels change to online OR RE(A) OR no setpoint\\par
\\tab calculated or temperature sensor failed or absent\\par
\\par
5.  average temperature (temp =RAT)\\par
\\tab One cycle average temperature is first calculated, cycle starts when isStartPulse = \\par
\\tab one or more channels change to online AND [RE(online) OR isMax occurs\\}\\par
\\tab\\par
\\tab After isStartPulse occurs, time and temperature are accumulated (totalTime and totalX) until \\par
     \\tab the next isStartPulse occurs.  One dt prior to that time, temp1CycleAverage = totalX/totalTime\\par
\\par
\\tab Then 5 complete cycles are averaged using RLS to produce temp5CycleAverage.\\par
\\par
\\tab if temp5CycleAverage = 0 (no average calculated), then\\par
\\tab tempAverage = measured temperature\\par
\\par
\\tab if the temperature sensor is failed or absent, then \\par
\\tab tempAverage = AVG_AND_SETPOINT_TEMP_ON_FAILURE = 70 degF\\par
\\par
\\tab isTempAverageReady \\par
\\tab set to 0 (not ready) when the Node goes into bypass (all 5 channels)\\par
\\tab set to 1 (ready) when the rising edge of one or more channels change are online AND\\par
\\tab  the RLS has completed 5  cycles OR\\par
\\tab  temp5CycleAverage = 0 OR measured temp is failed or absent\\par
\\fs16\\par
6.  Added in 4 element status vector\\par
Element 1 BitPacked values\\par
DryContact (1/0 = closed/open)\\par
temp1 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
temp2 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
temp3 status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
OAT status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
enclosure temp status (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
isTempSetpointReady (1/0 = yes/ no)\\par
isTempAvgReady (1/0 = yes/ no)\\par
relay1 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay2 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay3 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay4 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
relay5 failed (1/0 = failed/ not)\\par
PortalBypass (1/0 = bypassed/ online)\\par
\\par
Elements 2,3,4\\par
tempSetpointValue\\par
tempAverageValue\\par
Algorithm Version Number\\par
\\par
\\par
\\par
\\tab\\par
\\par
v42p6 changes: (all based on the most recent GUI changes, made by Max on 1/3/19 and several more made by Ric on 1/4/19)\\par
1.  GUI Modified to include CT rating (25 amp, 50 amp, or 100 amp) with default = 50 amps.  Gain and Offset parameters were also added to the GUI to linearly scale the current, default values; Gain = 1, Offset = 0.  Modified algorithm \"Unload Inputs into Globals\" to accept these 3 parameters and the raw current (sensor value) and produce a scaled value.  The CT rating is enumerated [0, 1, 2] = [25 amp, 50 amp, 100 amp] in Java before passed into the algorithm.  The algorithm operates on these enumerated values. A new output value \"currentNew\" was added and output from the algorithm to Java (Max has yet to present this value in the GUI)\\par
\\par
2.  Java modified to send in the relay status for each of the 5 channels.  They were checked by substituting a .1 Hz square wave to the yPaceVec and viewed on the debug output.  Comparison of the relay value with the yPaceVec values showed a 1 to 2 second delay but after the delay, they did follow the command signals (yPaceVec).\\par
\\par
3.  Java modified to send in the bypass command for each of the 5 channels.  This was checked using the GUI to switch between online and bypass and viewing the debug output from the algorithm.  \\par
\\par
4.  AlgoConfigFetcher.java, line 1552, I had to add in retVal = 8 for refrigeration, it was missing\\par
\\par
5.  AlgoConfigFetcher.java, some of the channel 5 signals were hardcoded to fixed values, I modified thise to accept the \"pref\" values like the other channels.\\par
\\par
6.  Corrected the refrigeration time table in the algorithm.  Checked tVec in all 8 applications in normal and extend successfully.  \\par
\\par
7.  Removed the limit on AppType for each of the 5 channels in the algorihtm, this is not necessary\\par
\\par
8.  Increased the \"starts per hour MAX\" value from 10 to 20 to allow heating tVec to operate properly.  Without this change, the tOn value was being extended for Apptype 5.  from 240 to 270 (extend mode).  \\par
\\par
\\f4\\fs22\\par
\\f0\\fs16\\par
\\par
v42p5 changes:\\par
1.  Short Cycle Controller Added chNo to each of the 5 controllers, used chNo to get the AppType for the channel, then calculated the tOnMin = min(tOnNormal, tOnExtend) and tOffMin = min(tOffNormal, tOffExtend) and used this as the On and Off minimum time limits. \\par
\\par
v42p4 changes:\\par
1.  Added \"offline\" status flag to Load controller if tstat or feedback temp sensor is not connected.  status flag is used in the cycler to close the relay if the Load controller is offline.\\par
2.  Current is liniearly processed by the algorithm (gain + offset), these 2 values are set from the GUI, admin, the processed current signal was added to the algoStatus.\\par
\\pard\\box\\brdrdash\\brdrw0 \\cbpat2 3.  Algo status vector of 15 elements is passed to the Java code in the \\f5\\fs18 CommArrayOut\\f6  (which had been used for zigbee energy calcualtions)\\f0\\fs16\\par
\\pard\\par
v0.42.2 changes:\\par
\\par
\\par
v0.42.1 changes:\\par
1. added the extern statements to the vsm file\\par
#define vsmHotLinkInit()\\par
#define vsmHotLink(s)\\par
\\par
2. changed the admin password to aaa\\par
Open the Android project and navigate to PACEApp/app/src/main/java/com/pacecontrols.pace4\\par
And open the file \\ldblquote HomeActivity\\rdblquote , this is a java file, the admin password is on line 128\\par
\\par
3. added debug statements and test that all input values are being input correctly\\par
\\par
4.  changed relayFeedback polarity because the input is 1/0 = equipment off/ on, in the unload sensor block, this polarity is changed to 1/0 = equipment on/off, this is the polarity used throughout the .vsm file.  \\par
\\par
4. check normal and extend operation\\par
\\par
5. check 30 min 3 deg logic\\par
\\par
Hitachi Release v0.3\\par
Restructured the algorithm so that the \"Load\" and \"Fan\" controllers are calculated first and produce tVec (3x1). The time vector triplet for each channel is then passed through\\par
 \"staggered start\" and \"Native Time Delay\" controllers.  Then all channels are merged and pass through a single \"Master Slave\" controller which produces a time vector triplet for each of the five channels.  The time triplet is then passed into a \"Cycler Controller\" followed by a \"Proof Controller\" producing the uPace (5x1) control vector.  This eliminates the need to process cycler signals for the Master Slave controller (because the time triplet is passed direcdtly to it).  It also eliminates the need for the 3 buffer functions (staggered start, master slave, fan), only the time triplet is adjusted for these functions now. \\par
\\par
Had to remove all \"section\", \"index assigned\" matrix operations from MS controller and the Time Table.  Was getting compile errors with the MS \"sectionj\" and \"Indexed assign\" present.  Was not seeing errors in the Time Table use of \"section\" but removed them to be consistent.\\par
\\par
Input vector changes:  No elements were removed, but some of the elements are no longer used\\par
Config Vector:  Was 30, is 15, don't use the MS2 elements, don't use the proof controller or bypass controller elements.  The proof controller and fan controller are always enabled. \\par
Active Channel Vector:  This vector was 10 elements, now it is 9 elements consisting of 5 for the thermostats, one each for Temp1, 2, 3, and one for the Current transducer.  The dry contact is always ready to accept an input and not included. NOTE:  all 10 elements are hardcoded to 1 (enabled) in this version. \\par
chxParameterVec:  was 28 elements, now is 8 elements.Now it just includes the AppType, Load controller thresholds, spans, sensor number, onTime boost, and native time controller.  The load controller is always enabled.  The native time delay can be enabled or disabled.  \\par
Sensor Vector:  was 19, is 17.  Does not use the \"Power Voltage\" and \"User Button\" inputs, everything else is the same. \\par
\\par
Added in the ability to restart each channel based on the online/bypass status.  When the bypass command changes from 1 to 0 (bypassed to online), the cycler is initialized to begin at tDelay to prevent short cycling .  BUT, the online/bypass status inputs are not being passed from JAVA so all 5 command values are set to ONLINE (0)\\par
\\par
The Fan is hardcoded to work in \"Manual Mode\", the only parameters used is \"FanControllerManualtimeDelay\" and \"Fan Channel Number\". \"Fan Enable\" is hardcoded to 1 (always on) and used in the Cycler controller. The Fan time delay is fixed at 90 seconds. \\par
\\par
Hitachi Release v0.2 \\par
Simplified the load controller in each of the 5 channel controllers.\\par
included SAT and RAT temperature checks to the 30 minute logic to place the PACE4 into bypass. Modified the 30 minute logic to cover the case when tStat always on but abs(SAT - RAT) varies from < 3 degF to > 3 degF and back to < 3degF.... (Hitachi found this error in their testing on 11/20/17)\\par
Hooked up dry contact screw terminal input in JAVA.\\par
Subtracted 25degF from OAT to account for relay self heating (this was measured) and forced the load controller to use the OAT - 25 deg signal for temperature feedback. In the bypass controller, forced the relays to remain OPEN when the algorithm is running and tStat is OFF, this is required to begin the Pace cycle with a tDelay, if not, it chatters.  \\par
\\par
Hitachi Release v0.1: (build as v35, internal 1.6.10)\\par
Applied the v0.44a change to all 5 channels.\\par
Modified the Bypass controller, it is always enabled (no GUI control over this) and also added in to go to bypass if the tStat ON continuously for >= 30 min is true and if the thermostat is NOT working or configured correctly, it goes into bypass (Bypass means to close the relay).  \\par
Modified the cycler, removed the tStat On time calculation because it is done in the tSTat ON continuously 30 min logic and added logic to only change tVec at the start of a pace cycle. \\par
\\par
v0.44a\\par
included the following logic on ChA only\\par
if tstat ON continuously for >= 30 min AND if abs(SAT - RAT) < 3degF (sampled at the 30 minute time), put the channel into bypass (relay closed).  Continue monitoring tstat, when tstat switched to OFF, release bypass and allow channel to operate normally again,  Also, when bypass is released, control begins with tDelay to prevent shortcycling.  \\par
\\par
v0.44\\par
corrected index for min ON and min OFF time used in master slave controller\\par
\\par
v0.43\\par
Load controller may select the temperature input from SAT, RAT, OAT, Spare\\par
Redesigned all controllers to not use matrix assign\\par
\\par
v0.42\\par
Corrected Load controller termperture inputs, they were not being passed.\\par
Removed the debounce\\par
\\par
v0.41\\par
Added a 5 second debounce to each of the 5 output channels to prevent short ON or short OFF pulses from being output to the relays.  This adds a 5 second delay to the algorthm.  \\par
\\par
v0.40\\par
Fixed the drycontact problem, operation now works in both normal and extend\\par
\\par
Set the enable for the Load controller, Cycler Controller, and Bypass controller to 1 internally, these controllers cannot be turned off from the parameter vector.  \\par
\\par
Native time delay, set the tOff minimum value to 2 seconds.  the minimum values for tOn and tDelay are both 0 seconds. \\par
\\par
\\par
Removed the buffers used for the master slave controllers and replaced them with vectors dimensioned to hold up to 240 seconds of history (4 minutes).  \\par
}
"
